   "sub_vi": "Thường, bật hơi, căng",
   "explain_en": "Korean has three of some consonants. Plain 가 is relaxed. Breathy 카 has a puff of air. Tense 까 is tight and short, with no puff. English speakers hear 카 and 까 as the same at first: that's normal.",
